{"step_index":1896,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-27T07:03:00Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-27T12:33:00+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-10-27T12:34:30+05:30\n\nThe command exited with code 0.\nOutput:\n125: Valid Palindrome \n def isPalindrome(s):\n    l, r = 0, len(s) - 1\n    while l < r:\n        while l < r and not s[l].isalnum(): l += 1\n        while l < r and not s[r].isalnum(): r -= 1\n        if s[l].lower() != s[r].lower(): return False\n        l += 1; r -= 1\n    return True\n\nprint(\"Is palindrome:\", isPalindrome(\"A man, a plan, a canal: Panama\"))\n704: Binary Search \n def search(nums, target):\n    l, r = 0, len(nums) - 1\n    while l <= r:\n        mid = (l + r) // 2\n        if nums[mid] == target: return mid\n        elif nums[mid] < target: l = mid + 1\n        else: r = mid - 1\n    return -1\n\nprint(\"Found index:\", search([-1, 0, 3, 5, 9, 12], 9))\n53: Maximum Subarray \n def maxSubArray(nums):\n    max_sum = nums[0]\n    curr_sum = 0\n    for n in nums:\n        curr_sum += n\n        if curr_sum > max_sum: max_sum = curr_sum\n        if curr_sum < 0: curr_sum = 0\n    return max_sum\n\nprint(\"Max subarray:\", maxSubArray([-2, 1, -3, 4, -1, 2, 1, -5, 4]))\n\n"}
